  <section class="lp-section" aria-label="Compatible foils">
    <div class="lp-container">
      <h2 class="lp-section__title">Compatible with your foil</h2>
      <p class="lp-section__sub">The Foil Assist works with most major foil brands via brand-specific fuselage adapters. AL masts support all brands listed. D/LAB has direct Duotone fit plus Armstrong adapter.</p>
      <div class="lp-compat-grid">
        <% %w[Duotone Armstrong AFS Axis Code\ Foils F-One North SAB\ Foil Lift KT Gong].each do |brand| %>
          <div class="lp-compat-brand">
            <span class="lp-compat-brand__name"><%= brand %></span>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <p class="lp-section__note">Fuselage adapters are brand-specific and sold separately. Check product pages for availability.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
      J. FAQ ACCORDION
  ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ %>
  <section class="lp-section lp-section--dark" id="faq" aria-label="Frequently asked questions">
    <div class="lp-container">
      <h2 class="lp-section__title">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="lp-faq">
        <details class="lp-faq__item">
          <summary class="lp-faq__q">Is the Duotone Foil Assist an eFoil?</summary>
          <div class="lp-faq__a"><p>No. It's a "Foil Assist" — it provides power for take-offs and light-wind sessions but preserves the natural feel of traditional foiling. Unlike a full eFoil, it's not designed for continuous motorised riding. You use the motor when you need a boost, and ride pure foil the rest of the time.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq__item">
          <summary class="lp-faq__q">How long does the battery last?</summary>
          <div class="lp-faq__a"><p>30–60+ minutes per charge depending on rider weight, foil size, riding style, and conditions. Using the motor in short, efficient bursts to catch waves provides the longest sessions (60+ minutes), while continuous heavy use results in runtimes closer to 30–35 minutes.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq__item">
          <summary class="lp-faq__q">Can I fly with the batteries?</summary>
          <div class="lp-faq__a"><p>Yes. Each battery is 159.6 Wh — designed to be under the 160 Wh airline limit for lithium batteries. Always verify your specific airline's policy before travelling, as regulations can vary.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq__item">
          <summary class="lp-faq__q">Will it work with my existing foil?</summary>
          <div class="lp-faq__a"><p>Most likely yes. The system is compatible with boards using standard US foil tracks. You'll need a brand-specific fuselage adapter (sold separately). Compatible brands include Duotone, Armstrong, AFS, Axis, Code Foils, F-One, North, SAB, Lift, KT, and Gong.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq__item">
          <summary class="lp-faq__q">What's the difference between Standard (AL/D-LAB) and Cruise?</summary>
          <div class="lp-faq__a"><p>Standard (AL / D/LAB) has the motor at the top of the mast — 17 cm below the top plate. It's ideal as a launch-assist for wave riding, downwinding, and wing foiling. The motor boosts you onto the foil, then the folding prop closes for zero-drag gliding.</p><p>Cruise has the motor at the bottom of the mast with an optional prop guard. It provides continuous, consistent propulsion — perfect for flatwater cruising, learning to foil, and rental/school operations.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq__item">
          <summary class="lp-faq__q">What's the difference between AL and D/LAB?</summary>
          <div class="lp-faq__a"><p>AL (aluminum) is the durable, proven option. D/LAB uses high-modulus prepreg carbon for lower weight, lower drag, and higher stiffness — the ultimate performance choice for advanced riders.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq__item">
          <summary class="lp-faq__q">How do I control the motor?</summary>
          <div class="lp-faq__a"><p>Via the Watch Ring Remote — a waterproof smartwatch on your wrist paired with a finger ring. Double-click the + button to activate, then press the ring to engage the motor. Release the ring to stop instantly. Multiple power levels plus a Boost mode are available on the watch interface.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq__item">
          <summary class="lp-faq__q">Do you ship across the EU?</summary>
          <div class="lp-faq__a"><p>Yes. Surf Store ships to all EU countries. Lithium batteries are shipped via ground transport in compliance with IATA DGR regulations. You can expect delivery within 3–7 business days depending on your location.</p></div>
        </details>
        <details class="lp-faq__item">
          <summary class="lp-faq__q">What warranty is included?</summary>
          <div class="lp-faq__a"><p>All Duotone Foil Assist products sold through Surf Store come with a 2-year manufacturer warranty covering defects in materials and workmanship. Batteries are covered for 1 year or 300 charge cycles, whichever comes first.</p></div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
